# Brewfile.linux — Linux-only additions, plus the Linux stand-ins for macOS
# entries that have no Linux bottle. Installed after Brewfile.basic and
# Brewfile.common on Linux; the macOS counterpart is Brewfile.macos.
# NOTE: Keep entries sorted A-Z within this file.
#
# Deliberately NOT here:
# - telnet: Homebrew has no Linux bottle (Tier 3, "no bottle available"), and
#   building from source is not worth it for a debug client. Every distro ships
#   one (`apt install telnet` -> /usr/bin/telnet), and `nc` from the netcat
#   formula in Brewfile.common covers the same "poke a TCP port" job.
# - inetutils, the other Homebrew source of a telnet binary: it conflicts with
#   the gping formula in Brewfile.common (both install a `gping` binary), and
#   .zshrc aliases `ping` to gping.
#
# Named explicitly even though silicon already pulls it in transitively: the
# pbcopy/pbpaste shims in .zshrc and the copy-mode yank in .tmux.conf both
# fall back to it, so it should not rest on a dependency edge. (Under WSL
# without WSLg there is no X server; both fall through to clip.exe.)
# Access X11 clipboards from the command-line
brew "xclip"
